{
  "project": {
    "name": "Dev-Board Tray",
    "slug": "devboard-tray",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "engine": "cadquery",
    "description": {
      "en": "A mounting tray that carries a microcontroller or SBC dev board on printed standoffs placed on the board's real mounting-hole pattern. Pick the board (Uno, Mega, Nano, ESP32-DevKitC, Pi Pico) and the standoffs land on the correct hole coordinates. Mount the plate to a wall with keyhole slots, bolt it down at the corners, or hang it on DIN rail with a clip foot.\n\nOfficial Visualizer and Configurator: Yantra4D",
      "es": "Una bandeja de montaje que sostiene una placa de desarrollo sobre separadores impresos ubicados según el patrón real de orificios de la placa. Elige la placa (Uno, Mega, Nano, ESP32-DevKitC, Pi Pico) y los separadores caen en las coordenadas correctas. Monta la placa en una pared con ranuras de bocallave, atorníllala en las esquinas o cuélgala en riel DIN con un pie de clip.\n\nVisualizador y configurador oficial: Yantra4D"
    },
    "thumbnail": "/projects/devboard-tray.webp",
    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "tags": [
      "arduino",
      "esp32",
      "raspberry-pi",
      "dev-board",
      "tray",
      "standoff",
      "din-rail",
      "hyperobject",
      "commons"
    ],
